  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "mein or meine? (revision of possessive articles)",
      "body": "In the last lessons you learned the possessive articles (*mein*, *dein* ...). Here you use them to talk about your family.\n\nFor **masculine** nouns use **mein**: *mein Vater, mein Bruder, mein Onkel*.\n\nFor **feminine** nouns use **meine**: *meine Mutter, meine Schwester, meine Tante*.\n\nFor **plural** nouns use **meine**, and the verb is **sind**: *Das sind meine Eltern.*",
      "ar": "mein للمذكر، meine للمؤنث وللجمع.",
      "table": {
        "head": ["", "Singular", "Plural"],
        "rows": [
          ["masculine (der)", "mein Vater", "–"],
          ["feminine (die)", "meine Mutter", "–"],
          ["plural only", "–", "meine Eltern / Geschwister / Großeltern"]
        ]
      },
      "examples": [
        { "de": "Das ist mein Bruder.", "en": "This is my brother." },
        { "de": "Das ist meine Schwester.", "en": "This is my sister." },
        { "de": "Das sind meine Geschwister.", "en": "These are my siblings." }
      ],
      "sup": false
    },
    {
      "title": "Plural-only words: Eltern, Geschwister, Großeltern",
      "body": "**die Eltern** (mother + father), **die Geschwister** (brother + sister together) and **die Großeltern** (grandmother + grandfather) are always plural. The article is **die** and you say **Das sind ...** (not *Das ist*).\n\nThe teacher mentions that in Swiss German you may hear *das Geschwister* for one sibling. In standard German, always use *die Geschwister*.",
      "ar": "هذه الكلمات تُستعمل دائماً بصيغة الجمع.",
      "examples": [
        { "de": "Das sind meine Eltern.", "en": "These are my parents." },
        { "de": "Das sind meine Großeltern.", "en": "These are my grandparents." }
      ],
      "sup": false
    },
    {
      "title": "Describing your family",
      "body": "To say how big your family is, use *groß* (big) or *klein* (small):\n\n*Meine Familie ist groß.* / *Meine Familie ist klein.*\n\nTo ask someone: *Wie groß ist deine Familie?*",
      "examples": [
        { "de": "Meine Familie ist klein.", "en": "My family is small." },
        { "de": "Wie groß ist deine Familie?", "en": "How big is your family?" }
      ],
      "sup": false
    }
  ],
  "mistakes": [
    { "wrong": "Das ist mein Mutter.", "right": "Das ist meine Mutter.", "why": "*Mutter* is feminine, so use *meine*." },
    { "wrong": "Das ist meine Eltern.", "right": "Das sind meine Eltern.", "why": "*Eltern* is plural, so the verb is *sind*." },
    { "wrong": "Das ist meine Bruder.", "right": "Das ist mein Bruder.", "why": "*Bruder* is masculine, so use *mein* without an ending." }
  ],
  "pronunciation": [
    { "de": "ä / ü in Väter, Mütter, Brüder", "tip": "The plural of many family words gets an umlaut. *Vater* becomes *Väter*; *Bruder* becomes *Brüder*." },
    { "de": "Cousin / Cousine", "tip": "From French: *Cousin* sounds like 'koo-zang' (nasal), *Cousine* like 'koo-zee-ne'." }
  ],
